  "problem": "The following table shows a proportional relationship between the weight $w$ (in pounds) of apples purchased at a particular supermarket and the total cost $c$ (in dollars) that customers must pay. \n\n| Weight ($w$) | Cost ($c$) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $3$ |\n| $4$ | $6$ |\n| $8$ | $12$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The unit rate is  $$3$ per pound.\n\nII. One pound of apples costs $$1.25.$\n\nIII. The cost of $5$ pounds of apples is $$7.50.$",
